			Ah, 'Proof of Human' — a name that screams 'we definitely know what we're looking for,' which immediately tells me they don't. As a PM, I've run enough hiring loops to know that the job description is the truest piece of fiction we produce, right up there with the Q4 roadmap. We put 'MTS' in the title and then spend six rounds trying to reverse-engineer whether the candidate can also serve as a de facto QA lead, a demo-day slide deck artist, and a therapist for the founder's ambivalence about pivoting. The name is just the first misdirect: we say we want proof of human, but we're really filtering for proof of availability to be oncall for the next growth sprint.

